 product council the  team's running migrations already in  progress suddenly saw huge optics and  adoption thanks to backpack this is good  they're getting more people to use their  stuff that's one of their goals but it's  also quite stressful because suddenly  you have 30 teams knocking on your door  saying oh this thing is broken on the  other hand one of our design goals was  to put the work for infrastructure  improvements on a small number of teams  rather than spreading it across the  entire company  so in some sense that was the right  decision so in the future we're going to  make clear which priorities are highest  for infrastructure teams and we're going  to continue to look for high leverage  work a small number of teams can do last  but very much not least the importance  of a pilot phase so I mentioned that our  original plan was you're gonna do  discovery we were gonna fan out test it  ourselves and then ship it to customers  but we realized that there was just no  way that we could assure our customers  or ourselves that this system was going  to be stable when we ship it if we  shipped it in this way so we didn't  delay GA significantly opting instead to  run a pilot phase for a very limited  number of customers and that allowed our  teams to be on the hook for reliability  without the same consequences when  things inevitably went wrong we're  running on a new cloud we're running  with some new infrastructure things are  going to go wrong we don't want that to  be a very public incident that knocks  out our entire European region this was  absolutely the right decision  just having wall clock time with real  customers that expect and accept  problems allowed us to experience both  bugs is on our side which happened and  incidents in the underlying cloud which  also happened we can never completely  avoid problems but at least we can  practice our response and now we're in a  much better position so here I honestly  don't know how we ever thought i